      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The draft board has been folded, the war room's coffee gone cold, and now comes the real work - turning promises into Sunday players. Washington sits third in the NFC East, six games back, with a 1-win streak and the cold arithmetic of a 14th-place playoff seed hanging over the building. That is not a contending position; it's a development mandate. <strong>The story right now is the rookie class, because this front office has to show it found not just talent, but answers.</strong> The Commanders need immediate help in the trenches, a receiver who can separate, and enough young depth to keep the roster from sagging when injuries hit. In this phase, draft picks are more than names on a card - they're bets on scheme fit, toughness, and how quickly they can survive an NFL Sunday. The veterans know it. The rookies will learn it fast. <strong>What matters next is whether this class can crack the depth chart by camp and make the staff look smart before the leaves turn.</strong>",
